{
  "description": "Asteroid taxonomy (taxonomy.class) -> mineral/ore composition. minerals_wt_pct sums to 100 per type. To get products: asteroid_mass x mineral wt% x typical_yield_wt_pct.",
  "units": {
    "minerals_wt_pct": "wt% of bulk asteroid mass",
    "physical.rho_*": "g/cm^3",
    "physical.macroporosity_pct": "%",
    "physical.albedo_*": "geometric albedo",
    "trace_elements_ppm": "ppm of bulk mass (g/tonne)",
    "typical_yield_wt_pct": "wt% of that mineral (approximate stoichiometry)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Mineral abundances are approximate; meteorite studies report vol%, converted roughly to wt%.",
    "PGMs and gold do not form their own ore body; they are dissolved in Fe-Ni metal (or sulfides) and recovered as a by-product.",
    "Types with confidence L/VL are team estimates based on tentative meteorite analogues.",
    "X (and the X part of any blend) must first be resolved by albedo: <0.075 -> P, 0.075-0.30 -> M (Xk if class Xk), >0.30 -> E.",
    "resource_presence contains qualitative, user-requested class planning assumptions. They may represent ice detections or interpretations on some class members, not measurements on every body. Null bulk_wt_pct means unknown; these flags do not add a second mass inventory or renormalise minerals_wt_pct. Hydrated minerals and free water ice remain distinct sources."
  ],
